historical id + name snapshots and a live `created_by` (ON DELETE SET NULL), a revision, rich content (≤100,000 
chars), optional summary, transcript identity, and nullable `room_id` (ON DELETE SET NULL); add note participants 
(user id + name snapshot, ≤50) and immutable versions (title, meeting date, participants, content, summary, editor 
historical id + name snapshot, live editor reference ON DELETE SET NULL). RLS scopes every read of notes, 
participants, versions, and items to `users.company_id = note.company_id` via `supabase_uid = auth.uid()::text` (never 
through `spaces`). `authenticated` and `anon` hold no INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on these tables. Historical and identity 
fields are immutable for every role (trigger or equivalent). Legacy-row handling: the migration refuses to run if 
`meeting_notes` has rows without a derivable company (SPEC §9 preflight).
