 158: ## T12 — Processing and Apply flow on the server
 159: Reasoning: Joins admission, dispatch, draft, authorization rechecks, and atomic Apply — the heart of 
FR-015–FR-021 — and owns every dispatch-dependent check (review P2–P5).
 160: Task: A start route that, in order: verifies the ticket signature and 24 h expiry (expired → rejected, no 
dispatch, even without records); compares the ticket's user/company/note with the authenticated application user; 
calls T9's admission RPC, which re-authorizes current membership and editor rights before anything else (existing 
operation → returns its pending/final/"discarded" status without dispatch, even if settings changed since; new 
operation → current membership, editor rights, and current settings revision required, stale revision → refused with 
the new provider name); dispatches once via T11 with the admitted snapshot and key; resolves suggested names locally 
(exact full name, else unique first name, case/accent-insensitive, current members only); rechecks membership and note 
existence before returning; honors client abort (operation "discarded") with best-effort outbound abort; and settles 
usage. An `authenticated`-granted Apply RPC accepts the edited summary and accepted items only at the draft's source 
revision, rechecks rights in the transaction, marks suggestions duplicating existing items, appends accepted items 
under T2's shared per-note lock and capacity, writes the summary, and creates one version — or changes nothing.
 161: Done when: Processing and Apply satisfy FR-015–FR-021 against the fake provider, including every 
dispatch-dependent usage, replay, and authorization outcome.
