in a single transaction holding the company settings row lock: (1) verifies the caller's current membership and editor 
rights on the note (for replays too); (2) looks up an existing operation for the idempotency key — if found with the 
same binding, returns its status without new admission, regardless of later settings changes; if found with a 
different binding, rejects; (3) otherwise verifies that the bound settings revision is current, reserves usage against 
the limit, records the operation with the provider/model/effort snapshot, and returns the matching key from Vault. 
Settlement once, against the admission day, by a `service_role`-only RPC; refunds only for pre-processing rejections. 
Idempotency keys scoped to user+company+operation and bound to note id, source revision, transcript identity, settings 
revision. Signed processing tickets (issue time, user, company, note, source revision, transcript identity, settings 
revision) with HMAC-SHA256 using the required server-only env var `MEETING_NOTES_TICKET_SECRET` (≥32 bytes, no 
fallback — AI start refuses with a configuration error when missing), plus optional 
`MEETING_NOTES_TICKET_SECRET_PREVIOUS` accepted for verification only so a rotation keeps outstanding tickets valid 
for their 24 h; the local value is provisioned in `.env.local` and `.env.example` documents it. A ticket-issue route 
(called when the notice is shown) authorizes current membership and editor rights before signing. Operation records 
without content kept 30 days (pg_cron cleanup); an operation without outcome 10 minutes after dispatch becomes 
"failed" and stays counted (pg_cron); deleting notes or users never changes usage; no client role can read-modify 
usage beyond reading its own company's count.
